[E0449] Error: `unsaid` keeps `self` in `labels`, and its signature does not say it does
    ╭─[ err/509_keeps_self_unsaid/main.wip:15:54 ]
    │
 15 │     fn unsaid(labels: &var Vec<Label>) = labels.push(Label(text: self.names[0].toStr()))
    │     ─┬                                               ─────────────────┬────────────────
    │      ╰─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── `self` is not in `keeps`
    │                                                                       │
    │                                                                       ╰────────────────── keeps what `self` holds or borrows
    │
    │ Help: say that `unsaid` keeps `self`
    │
    │ Note: a call keeps nothing of its arguments but what its `keeps` names, so that its callers know what stays borrowed
────╯
[E0436] Error: `labels` is used after `shelf`, which it borrows, was changed
    ╭─[ err/509_keeps_self_unsaid/main.wip:25:12 ]
    │
 22 │     var labels: Vec<Label> = Vec()
    │         ───┬──
    │            ╰──── `labels` borrows `shelf`
    │
 24 │     shelf.names.clear()
    │     ─────┬─────
    │          ╰─────── `shelf` passed as `&var` here
 25 │     assert(labels.len() == 1)
    │            ───┬──
    │               ╰──── used here
    │
    │ Help: use `labels` before `shelf` changes, or keep a value that owns its data
    │
    │ Note: a view points into what it borrows — a `str` into bytes, a `&` into a place — so that must not change while the view is still used
────╯
